[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains utility templates for generating PlantUML diagram
code. These templates are shared between pu_classDiagram and
pu_dataTypeDiagram and cover:
  - Diagram options (skinparam settings)
  - Hyperlink construction (pu_link, pu_attributeLink, pu_linkWithLabel)
  - Classifier node definitions (pu_itemDefinition, pu_classifierNameWithLabel)
  - Aggregation kind symbols (pu_aggregationKind)
  - Data type notation stereotypes (pu_dataTypeNotation)
  - Generation message header (pu_generationMessageDoc)
  - Attribute type with hyperlink (pu_typeWithLink, pu_internalLinkType)
  - Internal hyperlinks for named elements (pu_internalLink)
  - Conditional qualified class name (e_conditionalQualifiedClassName)
  - Whitespace removal utility (e_removeWhitespace)
/]
[module puUtilityDoc(
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
  'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[import ucmism2t::queries::elementQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::packageQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::typeQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::services::PropertiesService /]

[**
Emits PlantUML skinparam settings for class context diagrams.
Controls aspect ratio, arrow thickness, minimum class width,
legend and note background colors, class and package border colors.
Called at the top of every generated @startuml block.

@param anEObject - Any EObject; used only as a receiver for AQL
                   dispatch. The parameter is not navigated.
/]
[template public pu_options(anEObject : ecore::EObject)]
  ' HD display aspect ratio 16:9
  ' hyperlinkColor and pathHoverColor do not seem to work with class diagrams
  ' working approach: colors per item
  ' default font size for class names is 14
  
  hide circle
  hide empty members
  'scale 2
  scale 0.9
  
  skinparam {
    ArrowThickness 1.5
    MinClassWidth 150
  }
  
  skinparam legend {
    BackgroundColor white
    FontSize 10
  }
  
  skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor white
  }
  
  skinparam class {
    ArrowColor #404040
    BorderColor #404040
  }
  
  skinparam package {
    FontColor lightgrey
    BorderColor lightgrey
  }[/template]

[**
Alternative skinparam block using an explicit indentation string.
Used in contexts where the caller controls the output indentation
via the indent parameter rather than relying on Acceleo's automatic
prefix-repetition mechanism.

@param indent - Indentation string to prepend to each skinparam line.
/]
[template public pu_options2( indent : String )]
[indent/]scale 0.9
[indent/]skinparam {
[indent/]  shadowing false
[indent/]  minClassWidth 160
[comment][indent/]  minClassWidth 200[/comment]
[indent/]  sameClassWidth false
[indent/]  legendBackgroundColor white
[indent/]  ArrowThickness 1.5
[indent/]}
[indent/]skinparam class {
[indent/]  ArrowColor black
[indent/]  BackGroundColor ['uml-diagram-class-default-color'.getPropertyValue()/]
[indent/]  BorderColor black
[indent/]}
[indent/]hide circle
[indent/]hide empty members
[/template]

[**
Generates a PlantUML hyperlink with a visible label.
Produces the form: [[url label]]

@param url   - The target URL string.
@param label - The visible label text shown in the diagram.
/]
[template public pu_linkWithLabel(url : String, label : String) post(self.trim())]
  ['['/]['['/][url/] [label/]]][/template]

[**
Generates a PlantUML hyperlink with a tooltip.
Produces the form: [[url{tooltip}]]
Collapses multiple whitespace characters in the tooltip to a single
space to avoid line-break artifacts in the PlantUML tooltip popup.

@param url     - The target URL string.
@param tooltip - The tooltip text shown on mouse hover.
/]
[template public pu_link(url : String, tooltip : String) post(self.trim())]
  ['['/]['['/][url/]{[tooltip.replaceAll('\\s+',' ')/]}]][/template]

[**
Generates a three-bracket PlantUML attribute hyperlink with tooltip.
Produces the form: [[[url{tooltip}]]]
Used for attribute type links within class body definitions, where
three brackets are required to prevent PlantUML from interpreting
the inner brackets as a class-level link.

@param url     - The target URL string.
@param tooltip - The tooltip text shown on mouse hover.
/]
[template public pu_attributeLink(url : String, tooltip : String) post(self.trim())]
  ['['/]['['/]['['/][url/]{[tooltip/]}]]][/template]

[**
Generates the internal diagram hyperlink for a named UML element.
The link points to the element's HTML documentation page at
its #diagram anchor, with a tooltip showing the element name
and first sentence of its documentation.

@param anNamedElement - A named UML element to link to.
/]
[comment]
NOT USED. DEAD CODE.
[template public pu_internalLink(anNamedElement : uml::NamedElement)]
  [('../' + anNamedElement.u_path() + '.html#diagram').pu_link(' <U+2022> ' + anNamedElement.name + ':\\n' + anNamedElement.u_onlyDefinition())/][/template]
[/comment]
[**
Generates the internal diagram hyperlink for an association.
Produces an empty-URL hyperlink containing only the tooltip with
the association name and its first-sentence documentation.

@param anAssociation - A UML association to link.
/]
[comment]
NOT USED. DEAD CODE.
[template public pu_internalLink(anAssociation : uml::Association)]
  [''.pu_link(' <U+2022> ' + anAssociation.name + ':\\n' + anAssociation.u_onlyDefinition())/][/template]
[/comment]
[**
Generates a three-bracket attribute type hyperlink for use in class
body attribute lines. Only emits the link when the type has a
containing package (i.e. is not a primitive type at the model root).
The link points to the type's #diagram anchor with a tooltip.

@param aType - A UML type used as an attribute type.
/]
[comment]
NOT USED.
DEAD CODE.
[template public pu_internalLinkType(aType : uml::Type)]
  [if (aType.ancestors()->notEmpty())]
    [('../' + aType.u_path() + '.html#diagram')
      .pu_attributeLink(' <U+2022> ' + aType.name + ':\\n' + aType.u_onlyDefinition())/]
  [/if]
[/template]
[/comment]
[**
Generates an attribute type name with an optional hyperlink for use
in class body attribute lines in the diagram. When the type is not a UML
primitive type, the name is rendered in blue and followed by a three-bracket
attribute hyperlink pointing to the type's diagram page.
When the type is a primitive, only the plain name
is emitted.

The multi-line AQL expression inside each single block is wrapped
purely for source readability; each one produces a single unbroken
output line, avoiding the Acceleo prefix-repetition issue that would
arise if a call were split across multiple template lines.

The hyperlink follows the same profile-scoping convention already
used for pu_elementWithLink and RST cross-references: universe
diagrams (aProfilePackage = null) link to the type's universe page,
unchanged. Profile diagrams link to the type's own profile-scoped
page only when it's confirmed to be a dependency of that profile
(checked against DataTypes or Enumerations depending on aType's own
kind); otherwise this logs a warning and omits the hyperlink,
keeping just the plain type name. XMLSchemaDataTypes members
(e.g. XsdAnyUri, XsdDateTime) are treated as plain text with no
warning, same as genuine primitives, since they are never a
dependency of any profile by design.

@param aType - A UML type used as an attribute type in a class body.
@param aProfilePackage - The profile sub-package context, or null
        for universe generation.
/]
[template public pu_typeWithLink(aType : uml::Type, aProfilePackage : uml::Package) post(self.trim())]
  [if (aType.u_isUmlPrimitive() or aType.qualifiedName.contains('XMLSchemaDataTypes'))]
    [aType.name/]
  [elseif (aProfilePackage = null)]
    <color:blue> [aType.name/] [
      '../'.concat(aType.u_path()).concat('.html#diagram')
      .pu_attributeLink(' <U+2022> ' + aType.name + ':\\n' + aType.u_onlyDefinition())/]
  [elseif (aType.oclIsKindOf(uml::DataType) and aProfilePackage.u_childDependencySupplierDataTypes()->includes(aType.oclAsType(uml::DataType)))]
    <color:blue> [aType.name/] [
      '../'.concat('profiles_package'.getRequiredPropertyValue()).concat('/').concat(aProfilePackage.name).concat('/').concat(aType.name).concat('.html#diagram')
      .pu_attributeLink(' <U+2022> ' + aType.name + ':\\n' + aType.u_onlyDefinition())/]
  [elseif (aType.oclIsKindOf(uml::Enumeration) and aProfilePackage.u_childDependencySupplierEnumerations()->includes(aType.oclAsType(uml::Enumeration)))]
    <color:blue> [aType.name/] [
      '../'.concat('profiles_package'.getRequiredPropertyValue()).concat('/').concat(aProfilePackage.name).concat('/').concat(aType.name).concat('.html#diagram')
      .pu_attributeLink(' <U+2022> ' + aType.name + ':\\n' + aType.u_onlyDefinition())/]
  [else]
    [aType.logWarning('Type "' + aProfilePackage.name + '::' + aType.name + '" is referenced in a diagram, but is not a dependency of profile "' + aProfilePackage.name + '"')/][aType.name/]
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Generates the PlantUML 'class ... as' line for a classifier with
an inheritance-tree hyperlink. Rendered in the specified color and
with the specified prefix before the classifier name. Used for
super- and sub-classifier nodes in context diagrams.

The hyperlink follows the same profile-scoping convention already
used for RST cross-references: universe diagrams (aSubsetPackage =
null) link to the classifier's universe page, unchanged. Profile
diagrams link to the classifier's own profile-scoped page only when
the classifier is confirmed to be a dependency of that profile;
otherwise this logs a warning (a modeling gap, not something to
paper over with a link outside the profile's own scope) and omits
the hyperlink, keeping just the plain classifier label.

Confirmed against a real build: PlantUML diagram images always
render into a single, site-root-level "_images/" folder regardless
of where the embedding page lives, so the "../" prefix is constant
in both the universe and profile cases -- only the target path
itself needs to branch. Profile pages are flat siblings named
"[profiles_package]/[profile name]/[classifier name].html", unlike
universe pages, which nest by package.

@param aClassifier - A UML classifier to render.
@param color       - The font color string for the classifier name.
@param prefix      - A prefix string prepended before the name,
                     typically used for the package name annotation.
@param aSubsetPackage - The profile sub-package context, or null
        for universe generation.
/]
[template public pu_elementWithLink(aClassifier : uml::Classifier, color : String, prefix : String, aSubsetPackage : uml::Package) post(self.trim())]
  [aClassifier.pu_classifierNameWithLabel(color, prefix)/] [if (aSubsetPackage = null)][('../' + aClassifier.u_path() + '.html#super-class-hierarchy-generalization').pu_link(' <U+2022> ' + aClassifier.name + ':\\n' + aClassifier.u_onlyDefinition())/][elseif (aClassifier.u_isClassifierInProfile(aSubsetPackage))][('../' + 'profiles_package'.getRequiredPropertyValue() + '/' + aSubsetPackage.name + '/' + aClassifier.name + '.html#super-class-hierarchy-generalization').pu_link(' <U+2022> ' + aClassifier.name + ':\\n' + aClassifier.u_onlyDefinition())/][else][aClassifier.logWarning('Classifier "' + aSubsetPackage.name + '::' + aClassifier.name + '" is referenced in a diagram, but is not a dependency of profile "' + aSubsetPackage.name + '"')/][/if][/template]

[**
Generates the PlantUML classifier name with package prefix
if the classifier is from a different package than aPackage.
Used for conditional short or qualified name display.

@param aClassifier - A UML classifier.
@param aPackage    - The reference package for qualification.
/]
[template public e_conditionalQualifiedClassName(aClassifier : uml::Classifier, aPackage : uml::Package) post(self.trim())]
  [if (aPackage = aClassifier.package)]
    [aClassifier.name/]
  [else]
    [aClassifier.package.name/]::[aClassifier.name/]
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Generates the PlantUML 'class qualifiedName as "label"' declaration
for a classifier node. The label includes the optional prefix
(typically package name annotation) followed by the classifier name
in the given color. Appends the data type notation stereotype
(<<enumeration>>, <<primitive>>, <<dataType>>) for DataType instances.

@param aClassifier - A UML classifier to render.
@param color       - The font color string for the classifier name.
@param prefix      - A prefix string rendered before the name,
                     typically '<size:10>PackageName::\\n'.
/]
[template public pu_classifierNameWithLabel(aClassifier : uml::Classifier, color : String, prefix : String) post(self.trim())]
  [aClassifier.qualifiedName/] as "[prefix/]<color:[color/]>[aClassifier.name/]"[if (aClassifier.oclIsKindOf(uml::DataType))] [aClassifier.oclAsType(uml::DataType).pu_dataTypeNotation()/][/if][/template]

[**
Generates the PlantUML 'package qualifiedName as "label"' declaration
for a package node in grey color.

@param aPackage - A UML package to render.
/]
[template public pu_packageNameWithLabel(aPackage : uml::Package) post(self.trim())]
  [aPackage.qualifiedName/] as "<color:lightgrey>[aPackage.name/]"[/template]

[**
Converts a UML AggregationKind value to its PlantUML symbol:
  shared    -> o  (shared aggregation)
  composite -> *  (composite aggregation)
  none      -> (empty string, plain association)

@param anAggregationKind - A UML AggregationKind value.
/]
[template public pu_aggregationKind(anAggregationKind : uml::AggregationKind) post(self.trim())]
  [if (anAggregationKind.toString() = 'shared')]
    o
  [elseif (anAggregationKind.toString() = 'composite')]
    *
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Emits the PlantUML generation message header as a block comment.
Included at the top of every generated diagram file to discourage
manual editing of the generated output.

@param aNamedElement - The model element the diagram is generated for.
/]
[template public pu_generationMessageDoc(aNamedElement : uml::NamedElement)]
  /'
  PLEASE DO NOT EDIT THIS CODE!
   This code was generated by the Eclipse Acceleo module UCMIS M2T.
   Target language is 'Plantuml' generated on the basis of the model '[aNamedElement.u_model().name/]'.
  '/
  
[/template]

[**
Returns the PlantUML stereotype notation for a DataType subtype:
  uml::Enumeration  -> <<enumeration>>
  uml::PrimitiveType -> <<primitive>>
  uml::DataType      -> <<dataType>>
The result is post-processed by e_removeWhitespace to remove
Acceleo-generated indentation before appending to the class line.

@param aDataType - A UML DataType instance.
/]
[template public pu_dataTypeNotation(aDataType : uml::DataType) post(self.e_removeWhitespace())]
  [if (aDataType.oclIsTypeOf(uml::Enumeration))]
      <<enumeration>>
  [elseif (aDataType.oclIsTypeOf(uml::PrimitiveType))]
      <<primitive>>
  [elseif (aDataType.oclIsTypeOf(uml::DataType))]
      <<dataType>>
  [/if]
[/template]

[**
Removes all whitespace characters from a string. Used as a
post-processing step for pu_dataTypeNotation to strip the
Acceleo indentation before the stereotype token is appended
inline on a class declaration line.

@param txt - The string from which whitespace is to be removed.
/]
[template public e_removeWhitespace(txt : String)]
  [txt.replaceAll('\\s+', '')/][/template]
